Short:        Free bsdsocket.library and net tools
Uploader:     (We fill this in at upload time)
Author:       AmigaChrome Team
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      1.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.2.3, an AmigaChrome machine (see below)
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2
Distribution: Aminet

OpenSocket is a free bsdsocket.library for AmigaOS 3.2.3: the classic
Amiga socket interface that mail, web, FTP and game programs use, with
its own core library, the card's driver, a Commodity and the standard
network tools. It was called ACNet until 4 October 2026.

What it needs today
-------------------
OpenSocket's first backend, OpenSocket Host, sends socket calls through
the OpenSocket card of an AmigaChrome machine to real sockets on the x86 or
ARM64 cores it runs on. So today it needs AmigaChrome, with Network switched
on in Cradle (which then installs OpenSocket by itself). OpenSocketDirect, a
TCP/IP stack of its own for real Amigas (PiStorm first, then SANA-II
cards), is planned.

What is in it
-------------
Libs/bsdsocket.library       all 46 classic calls, none stubbed, and 27
                             later ones (BPF, routes, modern lookups)
Libs/opensocket.library      the core: status, interfaces, routes,
                             sockets, the event log, Wi-Fi requests
Devs/Networks/opensocket.device   the card's driver, with a SANA-II face
Devs/opensocketwifi.device   the Wi-Fi outside the Amiga, if allowed
Tools/Commodities/OpenSocketControl   status, Wi-Fi, connections,
                             diagnostics and the log (GadTools)
C/OpenSocket                 online, offline and status from a Shell
Tools/OpenSocket/            ping, traceroute, arp, ifconfig, route,
                             netstat, hostname, resolve, host, whois,
                             finger, telnet, ftp, tftp, sntp, httpget, nc

The tools stay in their own drawer, so another stack's commands in C:
are never overwritten, and OpenSocket never replaces another stack's
bsdsocket.library. On an older install it falls back to acnet.device.

